-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- Vim's HMS — Phase 5, OP-005: OP billing
--
-- `docs/prompts/phase-05-billing-rcm.md` §5.2. Eight new tables in `billing`,
-- joining the four Phase 1 already built for NC-001's cash counter (`payments`,
-- `payment_lines`, `advances`, `refunds`). Charges have been accumulating in
-- `billing.charge_intents` since Phase 2; this is what turns them into money.
--
-- Generated by `prisma migrate diff --from-url`, then post-processed to strip
-- the DropIndex statements Prisma emits for hand-written SQL it cannot see.
--
--   §A  row-level security
--   §B  the constraints that carry OP-005 §5's guarantees:
--         B.1  one master bill per OP visit
--         B.2  ONE CHARGE, ONE BILL LINE, ONCE — the idempotency index
--         B.3  Σ bill lines = bill total, verified by the database
--         B.4  a finalised bill is immutable
--         B.5  GST: intra-state splits CGST+SGST equally, inter-state is IGST,
--              and the three are mutually exclusive
--         B.6  requester ≠ approver on every discount
--         B.7  gapless invoice numbering per series per financial year
--   §C  grants, and the DELETE revoke that makes "never hard-deleted" true
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

